# Chapter 7, part 2: the menu and Edit / Preview / Print Document.
.h2 The menu of the Document Manager [str-menu]
.ix Menu entries, Document Manager
.ix Document Manager, menu
.ix Select Action
.ix Press Ins to Select Action
.ix Main menu, entries
The menu is the first screen of Strata.  Choose an entry with {k:Enter} or
{k:Ins} after moving to it, or move with the first letter (see
{n:str-keys-menu}).  The highlight starts on Edit / Preview / Print Document
and, after a
panel is left, comes back to the entry that was used.
.table 24 8 18
Entry | Key | Section
Edit / Preview / Print Document | {k:E} | {x:str-edit}
Maintain Dictionaries | {k:M} | {x:str-spell-words}
Compare Document Versions | {k:C} | {x:str-compare}
Restore Backup | {k:R} | {x:str-restore}
TeX Font Association | {k:T} | {x:str-fonts}
Setup | {k:S} | {x:str-setup}
Quit | {k:Q} | {x:str-quit}
.end
.pic pictures/str-main.png 4.8 The menu of the Document Manager.
A letter only moves the highlight; the entry is chosen with {k:Enter} or
{k:Ins}.
.ix Entry letters
.ix F1, main menu

.h2 Edit / Preview / Print Document [str-edit]
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document
.ix Document Name
.ix Working Directory
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document, panel
.ix Open a document
Edit / Preview / Print Document opens a document in the Editor.  It is the entry
that most sessions begin with.  When the Editor ends, the
Document Manager is on the screen again.
.h3 The Edit / Preview / Print Document panel [str-edit-panel]
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document panel
.ix Panel, Edit / Preview / Print Document
.pic pictures/str-edit-panel.png 5 The Edit / Preview / Print Document panel.
The panel has three fields.  Working Directory is shown first.  The focus
starts on Document Name, the field that is usually filled in.
.table 15 11 24
Field | Default | Meaning
Working Directory | see below | The directory of the document.
Document Name | the last name | The file name, with or without a path.
Variables | what is given | The variables of the conditional text of the
 | | document ({n:str-variables}).
.end
.rows 24 46
Working Directory | A directory name.  The default is the setting
 | workdir of the configuration file if it names an existing directory,
 | and otherwise the current directory at the time the Document Manager
 | started.  After a successful Edit / Preview / Print Document the
 | directory that was typed is the default of the next panel, until the
 | program ends (it is not saved: only Setup saves a directory).
 | A blank field means the current directory.  The directory must exist.
Document Name | The name of the document.  The default is the name given
 | on the command line, or else the name last used in this run of
 | the Document Manager, or else empty.  A name that has no dot in its last
 | component gets the suffix {c:.doc}.  A name that begins with a slash is
 | an absolute name and the Working Directory is not used to find it.
.end
The first two fields name files: the listing of {x:str-browse} is available on
them with {k:Keypad +}.  The listing of the Document Name field shows the
files of the Working Directory that end in {c:.doc}, in any case of
letters.
.h3 The variables [str-variables]
.ix Variables, panel
.ix Variables panel
.ix Panel, Variables
.ix Conditional text, variables
.pic pictures/str-variables-panel.png 5 The Variables panel.
The field Variables is not typed in.  It shows how many variables are given,
"none" or for example "2 given" (followed by the keys that open the panel), and
{k:F2} or {k:Keypad +} on it opens the panel Variables.  The panel has eight pairs of fields, Name 1 and Value 1 up
to Name 8 and Value 8: the name of a variable in one field and its value in
the other.  A pair that has nothing in it is not used.  {k:Ins} accepts the
panel and {k:Esc} leaves it as it was.
The variables are what the If markers of a document are compared with
({n:marker-variables}).  A name starts with a letter and holds letters,
digits, hyphens and underscores; a value is printable 7-bit ASCII without
quotation marks, up to 255 characters; a name that begins with a period belongs
to Strata and is refused.  When a pair breaks a rule the panel stays open
with what was typed and a box shows which rule: for example "The variable name
9lives must start with a letter." or "A value may not hold a quotation mark".
A value without a name is refused with "Line N has a value but no name."
The variables are kept until the Document Manager ends; they are not saved.
A change made while an Editor is running does not reach that Editor; it
reaches the Editors that are started after it.
Strata gives its own variables as well ({n:marker-special-variables}).
.h3 What happens when the panel is accepted [str-edit-accept]
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document, accept
.ix Cannot find directory
.ix Enter a document name
Pressing {k:Ins} (or {k:Enter} in the last field) accepts the panel.  The
program checks the fields in this order and, when a check fails, shows a
message in the footer line and stays in the panel with all the values
untouched.
.table 31 29
Condition | Message in the footer
Document Name is empty | Enter a document name
The directory does not exist | Cannot find directory DIR
 | (the directory of the path; for a new
 | name that is the directory part)
.end
The name is then made into a full path: the directory is joined to the name,
and a suffix {c:.doc} is added when the last component has no dot at all
(the name {c:notes.v2} is used as it is).  The Working Directory and the
Document Name that were accepted are remembered for the other panels of this
session.
.h3 An existing document [str-edit-existing]
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document, existing file
If the file exists, the Editor is started at once on the document.  The
Editor takes over the terminal (in the terminal version) or opens its own
window (in the X11 version, where the window of the Document Manager stays
and waits).  The Autosave and Autosave Interval of Setup are in effect for
the document at once, with no restart of the Editor.
.h3 A new document [str-edit-new]
.ix New File
.ix New File, document type
.ix Structured, new file
.ix Unstructured, new file
.ix Description, new file
.ix Author, new file
.ix Create a new document
If the file does not exist, a new document is made.  Two questions come
first.  The first is a list titled New File: document type.
.pic pictures/str-newfile-type.png 4.8 The type of a new document.
.table 15 45
Choice | Effect
Structured | A document with sections, levels and headlines.
Unstructured | A flat document of blocks (a memo or letter).
.end
The list is moved with {k:Up} {k:Down}; {k:Enter} chooses; {k:S} and
{k:U} choose at once (see {n:str-keys-list}).  {k:Esc} here goes back
to the Edit / Preview / Print Document panel with the values as they were.
When there are templates ({n:file-new-list}), the list of the type is
preceded by a list titled Templates.  It holds Structured, Unstructured and
each template, and the lines below it show the description of the chosen
entry.  {k:Enter} takes the entry and shows the New File panel; {k:Ins} takes
it and finishes at once, with Description and Author empty; {k:Esc} shows the
list of the type instead.  A new document goes through these questions
whichever way names it: a name typed in the panel, a name given on the
command line or a name chosen in the list of files.
The second question is the panel New File, with three fields.
.pic pictures/str-newfile-panel.png 5 The New File panel.
.table 13 47
Field | Meaning
Template | Structured, Unstructured, or the name or path of a template.  It
 | starts as the choice of the list.  {k:F2} or Gray + lists the
 | choices and a way to look for a template file in any directory.
 | A name that is not found gives the message "Cannot find the
 | template file", and the panel stays.
Description | The description of the document, kept in its header
 | (the field Description of the Save panel).  Up to 159 characters.
 | May be empty.  Default: empty.
Author | The author of the document, kept in its header.  Up to 159
 | characters.  May be empty.  Default: empty.
.end
{k:Esc} in this panel also goes back to the Edit / Preview / Print Document
panel.  {k:Ins}
opens the Editor on the new document.  {k:F1} on the New File panel shows
the help of Edit / Preview / Print Document.
.note The new document is only in the memory of the Editor.  No file is made
  until the document is saved in the Editor.  If it is never saved (quit
  with Discard), the file never exists.
.h3 When the editor ends [str-edit-end]
.ix Edit / Preview / Print Document, exit status
.ix Cannot run the editor
.ix The editor ended with status
After the Editor has ended the Document Manager returns to the main menu
and shows a notice only when the Editor did not end well.
.table 20 40
Status of the Editor | What the Document Manager shows
0 | Nothing.  The menu is shown.
127 | A notice titled Edit / Preview / Print Document:
 | "Cannot run the editor: PATH", {c:PATH}
 | being the Editor program of Setup.
other | A notice titled Edit / Preview / Print Document:
 | "The editor ended with status N".
.end
A file that exists but is not a document that the Editor can read (a
damaged file, a file that is not a document of this software, or a file of
a version that the Editor does not read) makes the Editor
write the file name and the reason and end with status 1; the Document
Manager then shows "The editor ended with status 1".
